From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:01:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 050/147] hjviewer: a new look, its theme and the home screens

The app kept RustDesk's look of 2022: Material 2 with a saturated blue, grey panels, square
fields, peer tiles in loud colours and, on Windows, Malgun Gothic. Now:

- common/hjv_style.dart holds the look: one palette per theme (the app icon's blue
  #1E6FD9 as the only accent, cool greys, thin borders instead of shadows), the radii, the
  text sizes, and a card decoration. The typeface is Pretendard (SIL OFL 1.1, Regular,
  SemiBold, Bold; the files come with the overlay in assets/fonts with their licence), so
  Windows, Android and iOS read alike.
- common/hjv_theme.dart: hjvRestyle takes upstream's lightTheme and darkTheme as they are
  and replaces colours and component shapes (app bar, dialogs, fields, buttons, menus,
  tooltips, switches, navigation bars, the window tab bar's colours). The roles stay
  upstream's: colorScheme.background is the frame, scaffoldBackgroundColor the content.
  MyTheme's named colours move to the new palette.
- Peer cards (grid, tile, list and the phone's list): a card with the platform in a soft
  tile of the peer's colour, the name in bold, user@host below. Upstream's builders stay,
  unused.
- Desktop home: the ID on a tinted card, the one-time password on a card, the connect box
  as a raised card with a filled field and 40 px buttons.
- Phone home: the remote ID on a card with a round connect button, a light canvas behind
  the cards, and the bottom bar's selected tab on a soft pill (activeIcon). The bar stays a
  BottomNavigationBar, which chat_model.dart and the phone's server page look up by
  navigationBarKey; its labels keep one height and take the theme's colours.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
